Package: libre-vmm
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, qemu-system-x86, libvirt-daemon-system, libvirt-clients, ovmf, swtpm, swtpm-tools, virt-manager, spice-client-gtk
Recommends: libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu, qemu-utils, vfio-pci, libre-vmm-guest-tools (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: looking-glass-client
Description: Libre VMM — A libre alternative to VMware Workstation
 A QEMU/KVM-based virtual machine manager with a modern egui-based GUI,
 REST API, CLI, and 24-architecture support. Built in Rust for security
 and reliability.
 .
 Features include live migration, GPU passthrough (single and multi-GPU),
 LUKS-encrypted disks, TPM 2.0 emulation, per-VM nftables firewall rules,
 cloud-init / autounattend.xml unattended installs, native Wayland support,
 and import from VMware (.vmx), VirtualBox (.vbox), Libvirt XML, and
 Quickemu (.conf).
 .
 Install libre-vmm-guest-tools alongside this package if you intend to run
 Windows guests — that package bundles virtio-win drivers, the SPICE guest
 agent, and WinFSP for shared folders.

Package: libre-vmm-guest-tools
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libre-vmm
Description: Bundled guest tools ISOs and installers for Libre VMM Windows guests
 This package bundles the open-source guest tools needed by Windows VMs
 running under Libre VMM. It installs them to /usr/share/libre-vmm/guest-tools/
 so the GUI can offer one-click access to them as a virtual CD/DVD.
 .
 Contents:
  * virtio-win.iso          Red Hat's signed VirtIO drivers for Windows
                            (network, storage, balloon, RNG, serial). GPLv2.
  * spice-guest-tools.exe   Clipboard sync, dynamic display resize, drag-drop
                            agent for Windows guests on SPICE. BSD.
  * winfsp.msi              Filesystem driver enabling virtiofs shared folders
                            inside Windows guests. GPLv3.
 .
 Install this package alongside libre-vmm to get one-click Windows guest
 setup. Linux-only users can safely skip it.
 .
 This is a single-architecture-independent data package. The Linux guest
 tools (qemu-guest-agent, spice-vdagent) come from distribution repositories
 and are not bundled here — install them inside the guest with apt/dnf/pacman.
